  "history_of_present_illness": "The patient is a 96\u2011year\u2011old male with a long history of type 2 diabetes, hypertension, obesity, and metabolic syndrome. Over the past decades he has progressed to stage 4 chronic kidney disease with proteinuria and micro\u2011albuminuria, and has developed anemia of chronic disease. He underwent coronary artery bypass grafting in the early 1970s and now experiences intermittent angina treated with nitroglycerin spray, but lacks guideline\u2011directed secondary prevention (no antiplatelet or ACE\u2011I/ARB). Alzheimer\u2019s disease with tacrine therapy contributes to cognitive decline and poor self\u2011care. Social isolation and limited support have resulted in a predominance of emergency visits (172 of 316 total) and minimal outpatient follow\u2011up. Current medication regimen includes metformin despite advanced CKD, highlighting potential prescribing safety issues.",
